# guestcrt.guestpe -- declarative source list for the guest x86-64
# guestcrt.dll: CRT primitives that MUST be real x86-64 machine code the
# guest instruction stream executes, because their whole contract is either
# the GUEST's own register file (setjmp/longjmp) or the GUEST's own call
# stack, which the dispatcher's frame walk has to see (_CxxThrowException).
#
# Every other CRT export in this tree is served by a spec2thunk trap stub
# that marshals to the native ppc64 implementation.  setjmp/longjmp cannot
# be: a trap stub would save (and restore) the NATIVE machine's registers
# and stack pointer, which is a silent wrong answer of exactly the class
# this tree's discipline exists to refuse.  And the 16-byte stub slot
# spec2thunk owns (RAW_BODY_EXPORTS) cannot hold the ~100 bytes each needs.
# _CxxThrowException cannot be a trap stub for a related but distinct reason
# -- see cxxthrow.c's own banner -- even though its body is short enough to
# fit a stub: a trap would raise the exception over the HOST's native call
# stack, and the search phase would then walk frames with no .xdata at all.
# So this module is built the way steamclient64.dll is -- see
# dlls/steamclient64/steamclient64.guestpe for the annotated original and
# the keyword reference, and tools/guestpe/guestpe for the tool.
#
# Nothing imports guestcrt.dll directly.  It is reached ONLY through PE
# forwarders (spec2thunk FORWARD lines):
#
#   game imports VCRUNTIME140.__intrinsic_setjmp
#     -> vcruntime140 guest thunk forwards to ucrtbase.__intrinsic_setjmp
#        (matching dlls/vcruntime140/vcruntime140.spec's own forward), OR a
#        prefix-staged Proton vcruntime140 carries that same forward itself
#     -> ucrtbase guest thunk forwards to guestcrt.__intrinsic_setjmp
#     -> this module's real code.
#
#   game imports VCRUNTIME140._CxxThrowException
#     -> vcruntime140 guest thunk forwards to ucrtbase._CxxThrowException
#        (matching vcruntime140.spec:2's own forward -- see
#        vcruntime140.thunks for the 2026-08-29 hygiene fix that replaced a
#        native trap line with this FORWARD), OR a prefix-staged Proton
#        vcruntime140 carries that same forward itself
#     -> ucrtbase guest thunk forwards to guestcrt._CxxThrowException
#     -> this module's real code.
#
# Both chains are ordinary PE forwarders the guest loader resolves itself
# (ntdll's find_forwarded_export recurses through chains), and the
# forwarder target loads from <build_dir>/dlls/guestcrt/x86_64-windows/
# guestcrt.dll (or $(libdir)/wine/x86_64-windows once installed) exactly the
# way steamclient64's directory-name contract documents.
#
# IMPORT lines: setjmp.c is freestanding register save/restore plus a
# DllMain that does nothing and needs none.  cxxthrow.c genuinely calls out
# -- see its own banner for exactly which two traps and why they are safe to
# use from otherwise-guest code.
IMPORT   kernel32
IMPORT   ntdll

DLL      guestcrt.dll
ENTRY    DllMain
DEF      guestcrt.def

SOURCE   setjmp.c
SOURCE   cxxthrow.c
SOURCE   exceptobj.c
